+# ARCHITECTURE: tagnotes
+
+Who owns what, and how the pieces connect. Each directory below is changed
+by exactly one owner; everyone else reads it and reports.
+
+## Owners
+
+| Owner | Owns | Exports | Handoff |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Owner A | `src/db/` (`store.mjs`, `store.test.mjs`) | `createStore`, `addNote`, `listNotes`, `tagNote`, `notesByTag` | `HANDOFF-A.md` |
+| Owner B | `src/api/` (`handle.mjs`, `handle.test.mjs`) | `createHandler(store)` → `handle({ method, path, body })` → `{ status, body }` | `HANDOFF-B.md` |
+| Piece 1 worker | `src/format/` (`table.mjs`, `table.test.mjs`) | `renderTable(notes)` → fixed-width text table | – |
+| Piece 2 worker | `src/export/` (`csv.mjs`, `csv.test.mjs`) | `exportCsv(notes)` → CSV text | – |
+| Integrator | `src/index.mjs`, `ARCHITECTURE.md` | `createApp()` → `{ handle, renderTable, exportCsv }` | – |
+
+`tests/app.test.mjs` is the end-to-end specification driven through
+`createApp()`; `npm test` runs it together with every `src/**/*.test.mjs`.
+
+## Layers
+
+```
+tests/app.test.mjs
+        │  createApp()
+        ▼
+src/index.mjs ──────────────┬──────────────────────┐
+   │ createStore()          │ renderTable(notes)   │ exportCsv(notes)
+   │ createHandler(store)   │                      │
+   ▼                        ▼                      ▼
+src/api/handle.mjs     src/format/table.mjs   src/export/csv.mjs
+   │ addNote, listNotes,
+   │ tagNote, notesByTag
+   ▼
+src/db/store.mjs
+```
+
+- **Coupled core**: `src/api/` imports `src/db/` directly. The API is built
+  on top of the store contract in HANDOFF-A.md (note shape, copy semantics,
+  `tagNote` error precedence, `notesByTag` never throwing).
+- **Independent pieces**: `src/format/` and `src/export/` import nothing from
+  `src/db/` or `src/api/`. They take plain note arrays and are unit-tested
+  with literal data.
+- **Seam**: `src/index.mjs` is the only module that imports all four. It
+  creates one store per `createApp()` call, wraps it with `createHandler`,
+  and re-exports the two piece functions unchanged.
+
+## The shared contract
+
+Everything meets on one data shape, fixed in PLAN.md:
+
+```js
+{ id: number, text: string, tags: string[] }   // tags sorted; fresh note has []
+```
+
+- The store returns copies (own `tags` array) of this shape.
+- Every API route returns this shape (or an array of it); `GET /notes` and
+  `GET /notes?tag=<tag>` return `200` with an array, oldest first.
+- `renderTable` and `exportCsv` accept exactly that array: `id` via
+  `String(id)`, `text` as is (CSV-quoted when needed), `tags` joined by `,`
+  (table) or `;` (CSV).
+
+Because the pieces consume what the API emits verbatim, `createApp()` needs
+no adapter between them.
+
+## Rules of change
+
+- A change in `src/db/` goes to Owner A; in `src/api/` to Owner B. Anyone
+  else who needs one reports it and the lead routes it.
+- A piece that disagrees with the core at the seam is fixed on the piece
+  side (`src/format/`, `src/export/`).
+- `src/index.mjs` only wires; it holds no behaviour of its own.
