+# HANDOFF-A: `src/db/store.mjs`
+
+Owner A's record of what `src/db/` now exports and guarantees. Owner B builds
+`src/api/` against this.
+
+## Note shape
+
+```js
+{ id: number, text: string, tags: string[] }
+```
+
+- `id` is an integer starting at 1, assigned in insertion order.
+- `tags` is always present and always a sorted array of strings
+  (`Array.prototype.sort()` order). A fresh note has `tags: []`.
+- A tag is a string matching `/^[a-z0-9-]+$/`.
+
+## Everything returned is a copy
+
+Every public function that returns a note (or an array of notes) returns a
+fresh `{ id, text, tags }` object with its own copied `tags` array. Mutating
+anything a store function returned never changes the store.
+
+## Exports
+
+| Function | Returns | Throws |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `createStore()` | a fresh store object (opaque; pass it to the others) | – |
+| `addNote(store, text)` | a copy of the new note `{ id, text, tags: [] }` | `TypeError` when `text` is not a string or is blank (whitespace only) |
+| `listNotes(store)` | all notes, oldest first, as copies (with `tags`) | – |
+| `tagNote(store, id, tag)` | a copy of the **updated** note `{ id, text, tags }` (use it as the `201` body) | `TypeError` for a bad tag; `RangeError` for an unknown id (see precedence below) |
+| `notesByTag(store, tag)` | notes carrying `tag`, oldest first, as copies; `[]` when none | never |
+
+### `tagNote(store, id, tag)` details
+
+- **Error precedence: the tag is checked before the id is looked up.**
+  1. `typeof tag !== "string"` or `tag` does not match `/^[a-z0-9-]+$/`
+     (so `""`, `"Not Valid"`, `42` all fail) → `throw new TypeError(...)`.
+     This fires even when `id` is unknown.
+  2. No note with `id` → `throw new RangeError(...)`.
+- `id` must be the stored number; compare is `===`. Pass `Number(...)` of the
+  path segment. Non-integer or `NaN` ids are simply unknown → `RangeError`.
+- Idempotent: tagging a note with a tag it already has changes nothing and
+  returns the (unchanged) note; no duplicate entries.
+- `tags` is kept sorted after insertion.
+- Error objects carry a human-readable `message` (suitable for `{ error }`
+  bodies).
+
+### `notesByTag(store, tag)` details
+
+- **Does not validate `tag`.** Any value no note carries – an unknown tag, a
+  malformed one, `undefined` – yields `[]`. It never throws, so
+  `GET /notes?tag=<anything>` can always answer `200`.
+- Result order is insertion order (oldest first), same as `listNotes`.
+
+## Behaviour changes from the previous version
+
+- `addNote` used to return the live stored object; it now returns a copy, and
+  the note carries `tags: []`.
+- `listNotes` copies now include `tags` (their own array per copy).
+- `tagNote` and `notesByTag` are new.
