+# HANDOFF-B: `src/api/handle.mjs`
+
+Owner B's record of what the API exposes. The independent pieces
+(`src/format/`, `src/export/`) and the integrator (`src/index.mjs`) build
+against this; they read only PLAN.md and this file.
+
+## Export
+
+```js
+import { createHandler } from "./src/api/handle.mjs";
+const handle = createHandler(store);   // store from createStore() in src/db/store.mjs
+handle({ method, path, body }) // -> { status, body }
+```
+
+- `createHandler(store)` — signature unchanged. Returns a synchronous
+  `handle(request)` function.
+- `request` is `{ method: string, path: string, body?: any }`. `body` may be
+  omitted on `GET`.
+- The response is always `{ status: number, body: any }`. Error bodies are
+  always `{ error: string }`.
+
+## Note shape (as returned by every route)
+
+```js
+{ id: number, text: string, tags: string[] }
+```
+
+`tags` is always present and sorted (`Array.prototype.sort()` order); a fresh
+note has `tags: []`. Every note in a response is a copy — mutating it does not
+change the store.
+
+## Query-string handling
+
+`path` is split at the first `?`: the part before is the pathname, the part
+after is parsed with `URLSearchParams`. Routing is on the pathname only, so
+`GET /notes?tag=phone` reaches the notes route. A `path` without `?` has an
+empty query. Percent-encoding in the query is decoded by `URLSearchParams`
+(`tag=Not%20Valid` becomes `"Not Valid"`).
+
+## Routes
+
+### `GET /notes` — list all notes
+
+- Request: `{ method: "GET", path: "/notes" }`
+- Response: `200`, body is an array of notes, oldest first (insertion order),
+  each with `tags`. Empty store → `200` with `[]`.
+
+This is the body shape `renderTable(notes)` and `exportCsv(notes)` consume,
+verbatim:
+
+```js
+[
+  { id: 1, text: "buy milk", tags: ["errand"] },
+  { id: 2, text: "call Sam, then Ann", tags: ["errand", "phone"] },
+  { id: 3, text: "untagged", tags: [] }
+]
+```
+
+### `GET /notes?tag=<tag>` — list notes carrying a tag
+
+- Request: `{ method: "GET", path: "/notes?tag=phone" }`
+- Response: `200`, body is an array of the notes carrying `<tag>`, oldest
+  first, same element shape as above.
+- A tag no note carries (including a malformed one such as `Not Valid`)
+  → `200` with `[]`. This route never returns `400`/`404`.
+- Only the presence of the `tag` parameter matters; `?tag=` (empty) is treated
+  as a tag no note carries → `200` with `[]`. Other query parameters are
+  ignored.
+
+### `POST /notes` — create a note (unchanged)
+
+- Request: `{ method: "POST", path: "/notes", body: { text: "buy milk" } }`
+- `201` with the new note `{ id, text, tags: [] }`.
+- `400 { error: "text required" }` when `body.text` is not a string.
+- `400 { error }` when the store rejects the text (blank / whitespace only).
+
+### `POST /notes/:id/tags` — add a tag to a note
+
+- Request: `{ method: "POST", path: "/notes/1/tags", body: { tag: "errand" } }`
+- The pathname must match `^/notes/(\d+)/tags$`; the id is `Number(...)` of
+  the digits. A pathname that does not match (e.g. `/notes/abc/tags`) falls
+  through to `404 { error: "not found" }`.
+- Status mapping, in the order checked:
+  1. `typeof body?.tag !== "string"` (missing body, `{}`, non-string tag)
+     → `400 { error: "tag required" }`.
+  2. `tagNote(store, id, body.tag)` throws `TypeError` (tag not matching
+     `/^[a-z0-9-]+$/`, e.g. `"Not Valid"` or `""`) → `400 { error }`. This
+     takes precedence over an unknown id.
+  3. `tagNote` throws `RangeError` (no note with that id) → `404 { error }`.
+  4. Success → `201` with the **updated** note `{ id, text, tags }`, `tags`
+     sorted. Idempotent: tagging with a tag the note already has is still
+     `201`, and the tag is not duplicated.
+
+Example: after `POST /notes` with `"call Sam"` as note 2, then
+`POST /notes/2/tags` with `{ tag: "phone" }` then `{ tag: "errand" }`, the
+second response is `201` with `{ id: 2, text: "call Sam", tags: ["errand", "phone"] }`.
+
+### Anything else
+
+`404 { error: "not found" }` — unknown pathnames, and known pathnames with an
+unsupported method (e.g. `DELETE /notes`, `GET /notes/1/tags`).
+
+## Status summary
+
+| Route | 200 | 201 | 400 | 404 |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `GET /notes` | all notes | – | – | – |
+| `GET /notes?tag=t` | matching notes (maybe `[]`) | – | – | – |
+| `POST /notes` | – | new note | `text` missing / blank | – |
+| `POST /notes/:id/tags` | – | updated note | `tag` missing / malformed | unknown id, or non-numeric id segment |
+| other | – | – | – | `{ error: "not found" }` |
+
+## For the integrator
+
+`createApp()` only needs `createStore()` + `createHandler(store)`; `handle`
+is what `tests/app.test.mjs` drives. The store dependency is taken from
+`src/db/store.mjs` exactly as HANDOFF-A.md describes; no change to `src/db/`
+was needed.
