+# PLAN: tag notes
+
+Goal: implement README.md § "The change" so `npm test` passes, including
+`tests/app.test.mjs`. `npm test` runs `node --test "src/**/*.test.mjs" "tests/*.test.mjs"`,
+so every new `*.test.mjs` under `src/` is picked up automatically.
+
+Split:
+
+- **Coupled core** — `src/db/` (Owner A, first) then `src/api/` (Owner B,
+  second, on top of HANDOFF-A.md). Each directory is changed by exactly one
+  owner. Nobody else edits either.
+- **Independent pieces** — `src/format/` and `src/export/`. They take plain
+  note objects and import nothing from `src/db/` or `src/api/`. One worker each.
+- **Integrator work** — `src/index.mjs` (`createApp()`), the seam that joins
+  the core and the pieces. Not a worker piece (see "Integrator" below).
+
+## Shared contract (everyone builds to this)
+
+Fixed here so nodes that never talk still fit together.
+
+| Module | Exports |
+| --- | --- |
+| `src/db/store.mjs` | `createStore`, `addNote`, `listNotes`, `tagNote`, `notesByTag` |
+| `src/api/handle.mjs` | `createHandler` (unchanged signature) |
+| `src/format/table.mjs` | `renderTable(notes)` |
+| `src/export/csv.mjs` | `exportCsv(notes)` |
+| `src/index.mjs` | `createApp()` |
+
+- A note object is `{ id, text, tags }`; `tags` is a sorted array of strings
+  (plain `Array.prototype.sort()` is enough for the tag charset). A fresh note
+  has `tags: []`.
+- A tag is a string matching `/^[a-z0-9-]+$/`.
+- The public store functions return **copies** (including a copied `tags`
+  array) so callers cannot mutate the store through a returned note.
+- `renderTable` and `exportCsv` accept whatever `GET /notes` returns: an
+  array of `{ id, text, tags }`.
+
+## Expected test state along the way
+
+`tests/app.test.mjs` imports `../src/index.mjs`, which does not exist until
+the integrator writes it. So for Owner A, Owner B and the workers, `npm test`
+**will fail on `tests/app.test.mjs` with a module-not-found error, and that is
+expected**. Report it as expected; do not create `src/index.mjs` to make it
+go away. What each of you must show is that `src/**/*.test.mjs` (yours and
+the existing ones) all pass.
+
+## Owner A — `src/db/` (the only node that changes it)
+
+Files: `src/db/store.mjs`, `src/db/store.test.mjs`. Output: `HANDOFF-A.md`.
+
+Changes in `src/db/store.mjs`:
+
+1. `addNote(store, text)` creates notes as `{ id, text, tags: [] }` and returns
+   a copy (today it returns the live stored object; with a `tags` array on it
+   that would leak store state). Existing validation (`TypeError` on
+   non-string / blank text) stays.
+2. `listNotes(store)` still returns all notes oldest first, as copies, now
+   with a copied `tags` array (a shallow `{ ...note }` would share the array).
+3. New `tagNote(store, id, tag)`:
+   - Validate the tag first: not a string or not matching `/^[a-z0-9-]+$/`
+     → throw `TypeError`.
+   - Then look up the id (a number, as stored): not found → throw `RangeError`.
+     Non-integer / `NaN` ids simply count as unknown.
+   - Idempotent: tagging with a tag the note already has is a no-op, no
+     duplicates.
+   - Keeps `tags` sorted after insertion.
+   - **Returns the updated note as a copy** — Owner B needs it for the `201`
+     response body.
+   - Internal representation (sorted array vs. a `Set` exposed as a sorted
+     array) is Owner A's choice; the public shape is what is fixed.
+4. New `notesByTag(store, tag)`: notes carrying `tag`, oldest first, as
+   copies. Recommended: do not validate `tag` here — a tag no note carries
+   (including a malformed one, which no note can carry) yields `[]`. This lets
+   the API answer `GET /notes?tag=<anything>` with `200`. If Owner A chooses
+   to throw instead, HANDOFF-A.md must say so, because Owner B's route must
+   then map it.
+
+Tests to add in `src/db/store.test.mjs` (keep the existing two):
+
+- `addNote` gives `tags: []`; `listNotes` copies `tags` (mutating a returned
+  `tags` array does not change the store).
+- `tagNote` adds a tag, keeps `tags` sorted (add `phone` then `errand`, expect
+  `["errand", "phone"]`), is idempotent, returns the updated note.
+- `tagNote` throws `TypeError` for `"Not Valid"`, `""`, and a non-string;
+  throws `RangeError` for an unknown id.
+- `notesByTag` returns matching notes oldest first, as copies, and `[]` for a
+  tag nobody has.
+
+HANDOFF-A.md must record: the exact signatures and return values of all five
+exports, the note shape, the error-precedence of `tagNote` (tag check before
+id lookup), whether `notesByTag` validates, and that everything returned is a
+copy.
+
+## Owner B — `src/api/` (the only node that changes it)
+
+Files: `src/api/handle.mjs`, `src/api/handle.test.mjs`. Input: HANDOFF-A.md.
+Output: `HANDOFF-B.md`. If something in `src/db/` is missing or wrong, say so
+in the report; do not edit it.
+
+Changes in `src/api/handle.mjs` (`createHandler(store)` keeps its signature
+and its `{ method, path, body }` → `{ status, body }` shape):
+
+1. Split `path` into pathname and query string (everything after the first
+   `?`); parse the query with `URLSearchParams`. Route on the pathname so
+   `GET /notes?tag=phone` reaches the notes route instead of falling through
+   to `404`.
+2. `GET /notes`: if a `tag` query parameter is present → `200` with
+   `notesByTag(store, tag)`; otherwise `200` with `listNotes(store)` (now
+   including `tags`). A tag no note carries is `200` with `[]`.
+3. `POST /notes/:id/tags`: match the pathname against `^/notes/(\d+)/tags$`
+   and parse the id with `Number`. Then:
+   - `typeof body?.tag !== "string"` → `400 { error: "tag required" }`.
+   - Call `tagNote(store, id, body.tag)`: `TypeError` → `400 { error }`;
+     `RangeError` → `404 { error }`; success → `201` with the returned note.
+   - A path that does not match the pattern (e.g. `/notes/abc/tags`) falls
+     through to the existing `404`.
+4. Existing behaviour is unchanged: `POST /notes` (`201` / `400`), unknown
+   routes `404`.
+
+Tests to add in `src/api/handle.test.mjs` (keep the existing two):
+
+- `POST /notes/:id/tags` → `201` and a body whose `tags` include the tag;
+  tagging twice does not duplicate.
+- `GET /notes` bodies carry `tags`, sorted.
+- `GET /notes?tag=x` returns only matching notes; an unmatched tag → `200`
+  and `[]`.
+- `POST /notes/99/tags` → `404`; `POST /notes/1/tags` with `{ tag: "Not
+  Valid" }` → `400`; with `{}` → `400`.
+
+HANDOFF-B.md must record: the exact request/response shape of every route
+(including the `GET /notes` body shape the pieces consume), the query-string
+handling, and the status mapping. The workers and the integrator read only
+PLAN.md and HANDOFF-B.md, so include the `GET /notes` body example verbatim.
+
+## Independent pieces (one worker each; touch neither `src/db/` nor `src/api/`)
+
+Each piece owns exactly the files it names. Import nothing from `src/db/` or
+`src/api/`; unit tests use literal note arrays.
+
+### Piece 1 — text table renderer
+
+Files: `src/format/table.mjs`, `src/format/table.test.mjs`.
+
+`renderTable(notes)` → string:
+
+- Three columns `id`, `text`, `tags`; cells are `String(id)`, `text`, and
+  `tags.join(",")`.
+- First line is the header `id | text | tags`; then one line per note, **no
+  separator line** between header and rows (`tests/app.test.mjs` expects
+  exactly header + N rows after `trimEnd().split("\n")`).
+- Cells joined by ` | `. Every column is padded (right, with spaces) to the
+  widest cell in that column, header included. **Pad the last column too** so
+  every line has the same length as the header — do not trim line ends.
+- Lines joined by `\n`, one trailing `\n` at the end.
+- Empty input → the header line only.
+
+Tests (`src/format/table.test.mjs`): header normalises to `id | text | tags`;
+line count is header + rows; all lines equal length; a row contains
+`errand,phone` for `tags: ["errand", "phone"]`; a note with `tags: []`
+renders an empty (padded) tags cell; empty input renders the header only.
+
+### Piece 2 — CSV exporter
+
+Files: `src/export/csv.mjs`, `src/export/csv.test.mjs`.
+
+`exportCsv(notes)` → string:
+
+- First line `id,text,tags`; then one line per note: `id`, `text`, and
+  `tags.join(";")`, separated by `,`.
+- `text` is wrapped in double quotes when it contains a comma, a double
+  quote, or a newline; inner double quotes are doubled (`"` → `""`).
+  Otherwise `text` is written bare. `id` and `tags` are never quoted (the tag
+  charset cannot need it).
+- A note with no tags has an empty last field (`1,buy milk,`).
+- Lines joined by `\n`, one trailing `\n` at the end.
+- Empty input → the header line only.
+
+Tests (`src/export/csv.test.mjs`): the two exact lines from
+`tests/app.test.mjs` (`1,buy milk,errand` and
+`2,"call Sam, then Ann",errand;phone`); a quote in text is doubled and
+quoted; a newline in text is quoted; a note with no tags; empty input.
+
+## Integrator — `src/index.mjs` (`createApp()`)
+
+`src/index.mjs` is **integrator work, not an independent piece**: it is the
+seam itself (it exists only to join the core and the two pieces), it depends
+on both pieces' module paths existing, and its test is `tests/app.test.mjs`,
+which is what the integrate/tests loop runs. Giving it to a worker in
+parallel with the pieces would have that worker building against files that
+do not exist yet.
+
+What the integrator writes:
+
+- `src/index.mjs` exporting `createApp()` that creates a fresh store
+  (`createStore()`), builds `handle = createHandler(store)`, and returns
+  `{ handle, renderTable, exportCsv }` re-exporting the two piece functions.
+  Each call creates its own store (`tests/app.test.mjs` checks two apps are
+  independent).
+- No unit test beside it: the README lists `tests/` as the end-to-end tests
+  through `createApp()`, and `tests/app.test.mjs` already exists.
+- `ARCHITECTURE.md` per the integrator brief.
+- If a piece and the core disagree at the seam (e.g. a field name), fix the
+  piece side; a needed change in `src/db/` or `src/api/` is a note in the
+  report for the lead to route to the owner.
+
+## Order of work
+
+1. Owner A: `src/db/` + `HANDOFF-A.md`.
+2. Owner B: `src/api/` + `HANDOFF-B.md`.
+3. Workers, in parallel: Piece 1, Piece 2.
+4. Integrator: `src/index.mjs`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`; then `npm test` must exit
+   0 with nothing skipped.
